    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T17:39:25Z",
    "body": "The maintainer, 2026-11-16, in chat:\n\n> \"There should never exist a case where the edge is treated as a bunch of small pieces like that..\"\n\nThis makes the scope a rule for the whole app, not a repair for one file:\n\n- A pickable edge is always a full feature edge. No model and no import path gives a pick of tessellation pieces or of short tangent-continuous pieces of one edge.\n- If a STEP file stores one smooth edge as many short edges, the import joins them to one feature edge.\n- If the import or `decompose` splits one curve, that split is the defect.\n- The rule applies to each consumer of edges: the pick, the chain rows, the highlight, and the chains that the operations read.\n\nDone means, in addition to the body:\n\n- A test over the STEP fixtures of the repository asserts that no pickable feature edge is a tangent-continuous piece of a longer edge (below an angle limit that the fix names).\n- `fig8.step` is one of the fixtures of that test.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
