    "body": "Diagnosis (issue-worker-high):\n\n- `fig8.step` has 70 `EDGE_CURVE` entities: 36 `LINE`, 30 `CIRCLE`, 4 `B_SPLINE_CURVE_WITH_KNOTS`. It has 30 `ADVANCED_FACE` entities: 10 `PLANE`, 10 `CYLINDRICAL_SURFACE`, 10 `CONICAL_SURFACE`. The file does not store short edges. The split is ours.\n- Root cause: `geometry::feature::chains` joins two feature edges only when they bound one planar face. The faces are exact-plane clusters of facets. On the crease between the conical chamfer and the cylindrical wall, each chord has a different planar strip on both sides. Thus no two chords share a face, and each chord was its own chain.\n- The edge above the chamfer joins because the top plane is one face.\n- Before the fix, on fig8: 1593 chains. The edge at z 19 (below the chamfer) is 719 edges in 719 runs, longest 17.22 mm. The edge at z 20 is 724 edges in 10 runs, longest 194.77 mm.\n- After the fix: 877 chains. The edge at z 19 is 719 edges in 10 runs, longest 188.49 mm (the closed r 30 circle).\n\nFix layer: `chains()`, because pick, highlight, chain rows and operation chains all read it. The PR follows.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
